            <ArticleTitle>Carbon dioxide embolism diagnosed by transesophageal echocardiography during endoscopic vein harvesting for coronary artery bypass grafting.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>683-5, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We describe a case of massive carbon dioxide embolism with an abrupt decrease in arterial blood pressure and continuous mixed venous oxygen saturation during endoscopic vein harvesting that was immediately diagnosed by intraoperative transesophageal echocardiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
